    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "-Share in the Spirit. Tradition and Cersprony\nThe Sydney 2000 Olympic Games take place\nfrom 15 September to 1 October, 2000 and will\nbe the largest cultural sporting event yet seen\non this planet. Air New Zealand is a member of\nthe Official Airline Team, bringing athletes and\ntravellers to Australia to participate in and\nwitness remarkable displays of teamwork,\nstrength and determination. Together, the team\nwill bring the world to Sydney to celebrate this\nmost enduring and admirable event of all time.\nPACIFIC\nCLASS",
      "A Supert Selection it\nAir New Zealand with the help of\nour top food consultant Tony Adcock,\nof New Zealand's famous Harbourside\nrestaurant, has spent the last two years\nassembling a dream team of chefs to\ndesign our menus. A team from around\nthe world with a flair for\nPacific Rim inspired cuisine.\nYour meals today have been\ndesigned to promote the culinary\nfare of the region and have been\ninspired by our contributing chefs\nin New Zealand, with an emphasis\non freshness and quality.\nEnjoy your meal\nPlease accept our apologies if\nyour first choice is not available.\nY2 NZ to AUS C1/00\n2007.086-008",
      "Contamporary\nbreakfast\nFROM NEW ZEALAND\nenu\nTand Deligh\nDeVcrages\nstarter\nFruit juice\nCereal and milk\nYoghurt\nSpiced fruit roll\nmain course\nCold selection\nSeasonal fruit platter\nOr\nHot selection\nHam and scrambled\negg croissant with\nhash brown potato\nTea and coffee\nlight option\nFruit juice\nCereal and milk\nYoghurt\nSpiced fruit roll\nTea and coffee\nwine\nAn award winning\nselection of still and\nsparkling wines from\nthe finest vineyards\nof Australasia\nbeer\nA selection of beer\nfeaturing:\nSteinlager\nwine\nDB Export Dry\nLow alcohol lager\nand\nbeverages spirits\nDark Rum\nBourbon\nScotch\nVodka\nBrandy\nGin\nsoft drinks\nMineral water\nOrange juice\nCola\nLemonade\nTonic water\nGinger ale\nDiabetic drinks"
    ],
